   "answer": "I fitted a 4PL curve to the standards of each of the nine runs and back-calculated the dilutions and controls. The LLOQ is 0.121 IU/mL (dilution STD*-7) and the ULOQ is 7.744 IU/mL (dilution STD*-1).\n\n**Two corrections to my earlier answer**\n- **Source of the numbers.** All numbers below come from the `fit_standard_curve` result under the recorded settings. I ran the fit again to confirm and got identical values. I ran no `compare_options` check, and no number comes from a comparison run.\n  - R-squared 0.9997 is the value for runs 1 and 5 in that fit.\n  - The figure 75 is the lower recovery limit from your request, not a result.\n- **LOD in runs 2, 3 and 4.** I wrote the comparison the wrong way round. In all three runs the LOD signal is below the fitted lower asymptote of the curve. The curve therefore gives no LOD concentration. The values are:\n\n  | Run | LOD signal (blank mean + 3 SD) | Curve bottom |\n  |---|---|---|\n  | 2 | 0.0719 | 0.0761 |\n  | 3 | 0.02725 | 0.0341 |\n  | 4 | 0.0136 | 0.0189 |\n\n**Settings**\n- Model: 4PL, with no weighting and no blank correction. The tool applied this model. It was not in the list of answers I received.\n- Standards: 10 levels, 2 wells each, per run. The fit used the mean OD of the two wells.\n- Blanks: 4 wells per run. LOD is the blank mean plus 3 standard deviations (SD).\n- Excluded wells: R7-LPC-2 and R9-LPC-1, the two wells you masked. Both are LPC wells.\n- Accepted bias of the standards: 25 percent. Accepted replicate CV: 25 percent.\n- Software: R package drc 4.6.1.\n- One replicate in the tables is one run: the mean of the two wells of that run. CV is across the runs.\n\n**Curve quality**\n- R-squared for runs 1 to 9: 0.9997, 0.9999, 0.9999, 0.9999, 0.9997, 0.9999, 0.9993, 1.0000, 0.9999.\n- Run 7: the 4PL gave a top of 5.169, an EC50 of 10.39 IU/mL and a bottom of −0.0024. The EC50 is above the highest standard (9.292 IU/mL), so the upper part of the curve is extrapolated.\n- Run 1: the blank SD is large (0.0645). Its LOD is 0.162 IU/mL and its curve-based LLOQ is 0.29 IU/mL.\n- Per-run LLOQ values from the curve are not the limits you asked for. Your LLOQ and ULOQ come from the dilutions across runs.\n\n**Dilutions and controls across the 9 runs**\n\n| Sample | Nominal (IU/mL) | Mean OD | OD CV % | Mean conc (IU/mL) | Conc CV % | Recovery % |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| STD*-1 | 7.744 | 2.8867 | 11.93 | 7.5869 | 11.07 | 97.97 |\n| STD*-2 | 3.872 | 2.2355 | 14.60 | 3.7072 | 8.73 | 95.74 |\n| STD*-3 | 1.936 | 1.5657 | 15.40 | 1.8719 | 11.39 | 96.69 |\n| STD*-4 | 0.968 | 0.9767 | 18.77 | 0.9171 | 10.93 | 94.74 |\n| STD*-5 | 0.484 | 0.5754 | 17.96 | 0.4637 | 9.21 | 95.81 |\n| STD*-6 | 0.242 | 0.3264 | 19.94 | 0.2334 | 8.79 | 96.45 |\n| STD*-7 | 0.121 | 0.1871 | 21.92 | 0.1205 | 15.71 | 99.55 |\n| STD*-8 | 0.060 | 0.1030 | 26.62 | 0.0558 | 15.55 | 92.99 |\n| STD*-9 | 0.030 | 0.0626 | 35.00 | 0.0266 | 25.89 | 88.71 |\n| STD*-10 | 0.015 | 0.0412 | 48.35 | 0.0139 | 42.04 | 92.56 (8 of 9 runs) |\n| HPC | 1.858 | 1.6177 | 21.49 | 1.9932 | 22.45 | 107.28 |\n| LPC | 0.465 | 0.5723 | 25.33 | 0.4569 | 20.03 | 98.25 |\n\nThe negative control NEG has no nominal value. Its mean OD is 0.1303 (CV 32.28 percent) and its mean back-calculated value is 0.0764 IU/mL (CV 38.48 percent).\n\n**LLOQ and ULOQ**\n- Rule: recovery from 75 to 125 percent, and CV below 25 percent for both OD and concentration.\n- STD*-1 to STD*-7 meet the rule. Their recoveries are 94.74 to 99.55 percent.\n- STD*-8 fails on the OD CV (26.62 percent).\n- STD*-9 fails on the OD CV (35.00 percent) and the concentration CV (25.89 percent).\n- STD*-10 fails on both CVs (48.35 and 42.04 percent).\n- LLOQ is 0.121 IU/mL (STD*-7). ULOQ is 7.744 IU/mL (STD*-1). The tool's own series limits give the same values.\n\n**What is uncertain**\n- The OD CV of STD*-8 (26.62 percent) is only just above the 25 percent limit. If you accepted that CV, the LLOQ would move to 0.060 IU/mL.\n- LPC has an OD CV of 25.33 percent, which is above the limit. Your rule applies only to the dilutions, so it did not change the LLOQ or ULOQ.\n- The two excluded LPC wells remove one value each from run 7 and run 9 for LPC.\n- Run 7 has an extrapolated upper curve.\n\n**Files**\n- Table: `across_summary_with_criteria.csv`\n- Curve plots for all nine runs: `fit_standard_curve-4/plot.png`\n\nNothing waits for you. I did not run a 4PL against 5PL comparison, because you did not ask for one.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n4 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-sonnet-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261009-084712-2345/work and wrote 1 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-sonnet-5-5/yun2026-lasv-elisa/run1/home/sessions/20261009-084712-2345/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Standard curve model: 4PL · Weighting of the standard curve fit: none · Blank correction: none · Average the replicate wells before the fit: signal · LOD as the blank mean plus k standard deviations: 3 · Accepted bias of a back-calculated standard (percent): 25 · Highest accepted CV of replicate wells (percent): 25 · Wells that you exclude as outliers: R7-LPC-2, R9-LPC-1.",
